==German==

===Etymology===
Originally {{m|de||*Hebanne}} from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|hevanna||midwife}}, later contorted to {{m|de||Hebamme}} to resemble {{m|de|Amme||wet nurse}}. This development is still reflected in modern German, inasmuch as the word can either be pronounced as a compound ("''Heb-Amme''") or as one word ("''Hebamme''").

